== 3. the three evidence agents on the 20 pilot levels under the registered conditions: cost, as bounds (EXPLORATORY) ==
  units: 3 agents (N, R, I1) x 20 levels x 10 seeds = 600, 20,000 actions each; a chunk holds 115200 worker-seconds; one session with the loop's largest gap at most 32460 s
  unit cap   300 s:  384 units per chunk,  2 chunks (Kaggle sessions) at most, 0.8 days at most
  unit cap   600 s:  192 units per chunk,  4 chunks (Kaggle sessions) at most, 1.5 days at most
  unit cap  1200 s:   96 units per chunk,  7 chunks (Kaggle sessions) at most, 2.6 days at most
  unit cap  1800 s:   64 units per chunk, 10 chunks (Kaggle sessions) at most, 3.8 days at most
  for comparison, the registered pilot agents of gate G1 (after the tag): 4 agents x 20 levels x 2 seeds = 160 units, 3 chunks at most at 1800 s
  engine time alone for 20,000 actions (laptop successors/s of logs/engine_speed.log x Kaggle/laptop ratio over 16 pilot levels; the agents' own computation is not measured on GVGAI and is not in this): at the median ratio 0.388, 4 to 38 s per unit; at the lowest ratio 0.099, 14 to 150 s per unit
  not runnable now: the kind gvgaiagent has no pins, image probe or dry run (rule R8; docs/STATE.md, amendment (ad), item 4), and no agent unit cap is fixed (gate G3 sets it from the pilot's times)

